    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42113" root="وعد" body-key="w">
    
      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اتّعد</span></b> , (A,) [aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَتَّعِدُ</span>,] inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِتِّعَادٌ</span>, (S, L,
K,) <i>He accepted a promise:</i> (S, A, L, K:)
originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِوْتَعَدَ</span>; the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span> being changed into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span>
and then incorporated [into the augmentative
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span>]: some persons say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ٱئْتَعَدَ</span>, aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَأْتَعِدُ</span>, (inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ٱئْتِعَادٌ</span>, TA) and pronounce the act. part. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤْتَعِدٌ</span>, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ء</span>; (S, L, K;) like as they say
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَأْتَسِرُ</span>: (S, L:) but [if they do not change the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">و</span>
into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span>] they should say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِيتَعَدَ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَاتَعِدُ</span>, and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُوتَعِدٌ</span>, without 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَعُدَ</span></b> . (IB, L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, <i>He confided in the promise of another.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See
also 1: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  and 6.

